# 02 — Task loop

<!-- GEN: Why: task-by-task grounding is what prevents bulk coding and scope creep. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

<!-- GEN: Rules I4, I5, I6 with the workspace's task format and task-level commands (06). -->

**Never code several tasks in one pass.** Take the phase's tasks top to bottom:

## A. Read & ground the task

- Open `{{phase_pattern}}`; take the next unticked task (`{{task_unticked}}`).
- Confirm every earlier task is ticked (`{{task_ticked}}`).
- Note: target files, reused components/contracts, signatures it must produce, acceptance criteria.

## B. Implement only that task

- Write or modify **only** the task's files.
- Use the components and conventions the design mapped; placement per {{clean_architecture_link}}, code style per {{clean_code_link}}, tests per {{unit_test_link}}.
- A mapped component or contract that does not fit → stop, report a planning blocker to {{planner_role}}.

## C. Check immediately

Run the task's own check before moving on (see {{ref_06}}):

```
{{task_check_example}}
```

Fix errors now; never carry a red check into the next task.

## D. Tick and re-ground

- Tick the task in the phase file.
- **Re-read the phase file** for the next task (scope, reuse, signatures, acceptance) before touching code.

